      "rejected_notes": [
        "Baseline and climatology are part of the answer: build RECON_9120 against a 1991-2020 monthly climatology and RECON_8110 against 1981-2010, each month matched to its own calendar month (removes the seasonal cycle); the result's attrs record both. The two CPC products differ in baseline and are not interchangeable.",
        "The 81-10 minus 91-20 difference between two series of the same index is one constant offset per calendar month, not an error: report the published CPC offset and compare the RECON offset to it; do not read a residual mismatch as a reconstruction error. Events are defined by persistence — count El Nino from the 3-month running mean only where values stay ≥ +0.5 °C (La Nina ≤ -0.5 °C) for at least 5 consecutive overlapping seasons (`min_duration`); a single step beyond threshold is noise."
      ]
